1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,122
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,170 --> 00:00:04,763
DWIGHT: It's
you. It's really you.

3
00:00:05,105 --> 00:00:06,105
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

4
00:00:07,574 --> 00:00:09,941
Oh, no. Somebody help!

5
00:00:10,844 --> 00:00:12,904
Penguin. He
killed the librarian.

6
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,244
I don't wanna kill him.
I want to destroy him!

7
00:00:16,483 --> 00:00:19,681
GUS: <i>And you promised them
Jerome. They want to see his face!</i>

8
00:00:19,853 --> 00:00:21,947
DWIGHT: <i>Behold, the prophet.</i>

9
00:00:22,122 --> 00:00:23,420
ALL: We are Jerome!

10
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:25,889
You get the message? We
don't work for you no more.

11
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:27,357
COBBLEPOT: I will gut you!

12
00:00:27,528 --> 00:00:29,394
- Then Nygma dies.
- They have Ed.

13
00:00:30,197 --> 00:00:31,957
JEROME: <i>When I was
last, you know, uh, alive,</i>

14
00:00:32,099 --> 00:00:33,376
<i>I was about to kill Bruce Wayne.</i>

15
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:34,868
Well, where is my face?

16
00:00:35,168 --> 00:00:36,636
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

17
00:00:36,870 --> 00:00:38,202
- What?
- ED: <i>Oswald.</i>

18
00:00:38,372 --> 00:00:40,364
- Where are you?
<i>- Cane Chemicals.</i>

19
00:00:40,541 --> 00:00:41,941
<i>Oswald, hurry, please...</i>

20
00:00:42,576 --> 00:00:44,943
JEROME: <i>Tonight,
Gotham, there are no rules.</i>

21
00:00:45,112 --> 00:00:49,709
<i>And when morning comes...
You, too, shall be reborn.</i>

22
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:51,017
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

23
00:00:51,218 --> 00:00:53,018
JIM: <i>He's at the power
plant across the river.</i>

24
00:01:02,329 --> 00:01:04,457
- (MEN SHOUTING)
- (MAN LAUGHS MANIACALLY)

25
00:01:07,334 --> 00:01:08,927
Get those freaks in the cages.

26
00:01:09,102 --> 00:01:10,229
We need to find Jerome.

27
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:12,831
Hey! Watch him!

28
00:01:18,378 --> 00:01:19,378
(GRUNTS)

29
00:01:22,316 --> 00:01:24,376
What about you? Do you
know where Jerome is?

30
00:01:24,551 --> 00:01:27,350
- Where is he?
- Where is he? Look around.

31
00:01:27,521 --> 00:01:28,819
He's everywhere!

32
00:01:29,456 --> 00:01:31,516
MAN: <i>Incoming! Get up.</i>

33
00:01:37,064 --> 00:01:38,191
Tonight,

34
00:01:38,365 --> 00:01:41,392
Gotham is awakened!

35
00:01:42,235 --> 00:01:43,726
(LAUGHING MANIACALLY)

36
00:01:45,405 --> 00:01:47,431
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

37
00:01:52,112 --> 00:01:54,152
(HUFFING) Remember,
Ed's safety is all that matters.

38
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:56,613
Whoever took him will pay,
but only once Ed is back.

39
00:01:58,719 --> 00:01:59,778
Ed?

40
00:02:00,921 --> 00:02:02,253
Edward?

41
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:10,896
Ed?

42
00:02:11,498 --> 00:02:12,966
(PANTING)

43
00:02:15,035 --> 00:02:17,004
Are you all right?
Tell me you're all right.

44
00:02:17,170 --> 00:02:19,401
- I'm fine, Oswald.
- (LAUGHS)

45
00:02:19,640 --> 00:02:21,939
Of course you are.
Where are they?

46
00:02:22,643 --> 00:02:25,112
Who dared to think they
could lay their hands on you?

47
00:02:25,278 --> 00:02:26,302
I'm alone.

48
00:02:27,414 --> 00:02:29,007
(CHUCKLES) You escaped?

49
00:02:29,182 --> 00:02:31,344
Yeah, you did, didn't
you? You rascal!

50
00:02:32,185 --> 00:02:34,848
- Did you bring anyone else?
- What? Why? No...

51
00:02:37,791 --> 00:02:39,623
Just wondering if I was
gonna have to reload.

52
00:02:41,128 --> 00:02:43,791
- I don't understand.
- I know.

53
00:02:44,898 --> 00:02:46,093
That's been half the fun.

54
00:02:47,267 --> 00:02:48,394
I'm sorry, I...

55
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:52,502
What is happening? I...
You weren't kidnapped?

56
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:54,642
Not unless you count
kidnapping yourself.

57
00:02:57,644 --> 00:02:58,668
Recognize it?

58
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:02,540
But, why should you? I doubt
you did the deed yourself.

59
00:03:02,849 --> 00:03:05,216
That car belonged to Isabella.

60
00:03:06,987 --> 00:03:08,888
Ed. Whatever you've heard...

61
00:03:09,089 --> 00:03:10,089
(GRUNTS)

62
00:03:10,691 --> 00:03:12,284
I know it was you, Oswald.

63
00:03:14,161 --> 00:03:16,960
Isabella was my everything,
and you took her from me.

64
00:03:18,098 --> 00:03:19,698
And now, I've taken
everything from you.

65
00:03:22,035 --> 00:03:23,435
Well, almost everything.

66
00:03:24,438 --> 00:03:25,804
<i>You still have your life</i>

67
00:03:26,807 --> 00:03:28,537
but that ends tonight!

68
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:34,772
MAN: (ON SPEAKER) <i>Attention,
all residents. Stay off the streets...</i>

69
00:03:35,248 --> 00:03:39,481
<i>A curfew is in effect for
Gotham City until further notice.</i>

70
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:42,985
Seems like judgment came to
Gotham earlier than expected.

71
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:47,085
If the situation worsens,
we may be forced to step in.

72
00:03:47,294 --> 00:03:48,819
(EXPLOSIONS IN THE DISTANCE)

73
00:03:49,463 --> 00:03:51,989
The city will bend
long before it breaks.

74
00:03:52,632 --> 00:03:54,362
Give the GCPD a chance.

75
00:03:54,534 --> 00:03:57,163
Your faith in him is touching.

76
00:03:59,106 --> 00:04:00,699
And possibly dangerous.

77
00:04:02,676 --> 00:04:05,145
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING, LAUGHTER)

78
00:04:06,413 --> 00:04:08,939
We're getting reports of a
riot growing on the west side,

79
00:04:09,116 --> 00:04:10,880
as well as widespread
looting uptown.

80
00:04:11,384 --> 00:04:13,785
Mobs of cult members
have taken over Anders Park,

81
00:04:13,954 --> 00:04:15,684
Gotham Cathedral... The zoo?

82
00:04:15,856 --> 00:04:18,018
All right. Concentrate
units on the west side.

83
00:04:18,191 --> 00:04:21,389
Make sure they're issued riot
gear. Any word on Jerome Valeska?

84
00:04:21,661 --> 00:04:22,685
Nothing yet.

85
00:04:23,396 --> 00:04:24,836
Let me know as
soon as he's spotted.

86
00:04:25,932 --> 00:04:26,956
Right. Got it.

87
00:04:27,467 --> 00:04:29,936
Lights aren't coming back
tonight. Tomorrow, if we're lucky.

88
00:04:30,103 --> 00:04:32,834
This thing just keeps getting
bigger. It's not just the cult anymore.

89
00:04:33,006 --> 00:04:34,838
Ordinary citizens are
taking Jerome's cue.

90
00:04:35,008 --> 00:04:36,786
- (TELEPHONE RINGING)
- Meanwhile Cobblepot's MIA.

91
00:04:36,810 --> 00:04:39,055
You call down to City Hall,
and literally no one's in charge.

92
00:04:39,079 --> 00:04:40,945
Although that might
actually be good news.

93
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:43,379
We need to find
Jerome. He's the symbol.

94
00:04:43,550 --> 00:04:46,452
If we can take him out, maybe we
can limit this to a single bad night.

95
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,264
Now how the hell are we
supposed to find him out there?

96
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,600
- The city's one giant dumpster fire.
- (TELEPHONE CONTINUES RINGING)

97
00:04:50,624 --> 00:04:52,635
Jerome said he wanted to
plunge the city into darkness

98
00:04:52,659 --> 00:04:54,070
so people could do
what they want, right?

99
00:04:54,094 --> 00:04:56,414
He's not one to miss out on
the fun. So, what does he want?

100
00:04:56,530 --> 00:04:59,523
A puppy? How the hell should
I know? I didn't talk to him.

101
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:02,193
- (TELEPHONE CONTINUES RINGING)
- No. But Lee did.

102
00:05:03,069 --> 00:05:04,069
Yes?

103
00:05:04,237 --> 00:05:06,763
Listen, my father
appeared to me. (GRUNTS)

104
00:05:07,774 --> 00:05:08,774
I saw him.

105
00:05:09,342 --> 00:05:10,342
No.

106
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:13,844
You saw a man that
I met in Indian Hill.

107
00:05:14,548 --> 00:05:15,811
Does killer impersonations.

108
00:05:17,217 --> 00:05:18,412
You see, Oswald,

109
00:05:19,152 --> 00:05:20,313
how do I put this?

110
00:05:21,755 --> 00:05:22,916
Ghosts aren't real.

111
00:05:23,924 --> 00:05:27,361
But my father's remains?
You stole them from his grave?

112
00:05:27,694 --> 00:05:30,163
Yep. Don't worry.

113
00:05:30,864 --> 00:05:31,991
He's at peace now.

114
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:36,466
I gently placed his remains inside a
dumpster behind a Chinese restaurant.

115
00:05:38,939 --> 00:05:42,034
You were angry. I
understand. I even forgive you.

116
00:05:42,776 --> 00:05:44,768
But, but killing
me is not the way.

117
00:05:44,945 --> 00:05:46,914
So, you admit
you killed Isabella.

118
00:05:48,381 --> 00:05:50,976
- Fine. Is that what you want?
- Yes!

119
00:05:51,418 --> 00:05:53,717
I confess, I had her killed.

120
00:05:54,888 --> 00:05:57,619
But guess what?
You should thank me.

121
00:05:58,592 --> 00:06:00,873
Because we both know what
would have happened if I hadn't.

122
00:06:00,994 --> 00:06:01,994
Yes!

123
00:06:02,162 --> 00:06:04,290
I could have lived a life
with the woman I loved.

124
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:06,997
I could've been happy.

125
00:06:07,567 --> 00:06:10,366
No, Ed. You would
have killed her.

126
00:06:12,572 --> 00:06:16,168
Just like you did the other
one. You couldn't have helped it.

127
00:06:16,843 --> 00:06:18,971
And afterward, you
would have hated yourself.

128
00:06:20,881 --> 00:06:21,881
Well,

129
00:06:23,083 --> 00:06:24,415
we'll never know, will we?

130
00:06:25,619 --> 00:06:26,917
I did it for love.

131
00:06:30,490 --> 00:06:31,514
What?

132
00:06:32,325 --> 00:06:33,725
I did it because I love you.

133
00:06:35,228 --> 00:06:36,628
- You should know that.
- Shut up!

134
00:06:39,833 --> 00:06:41,324
Love is about sacrifice.

135
00:06:42,068 --> 00:06:44,867
It's about putting someone else's
needs and happiness before your own.

136
00:06:45,038 --> 00:06:47,303
- Ed, please.
- The truth is, Oswald,

137
00:06:47,474 --> 00:06:49,739
you would sacrifice anyone
to save your own neck.

138
00:06:51,344 --> 00:06:53,745
Even me. Now.

139
00:06:54,047 --> 00:06:55,276
If you'll look above us,

140
00:06:55,448 --> 00:06:58,509
you'll see a cauldron
of highly corrosive acid

141
00:06:59,219 --> 00:07:01,984
which is currently being
held in place by this chain.

142
00:07:04,557 --> 00:07:06,890
When the ice melts,
the chain comes loose,

143
00:07:07,961 --> 00:07:09,361
the vat of acid tips.

144
00:07:10,297 --> 00:07:11,297
You get the idea.

145
00:07:11,665 --> 00:07:12,945
- (VALVE SQUEAKS)
- (GAS HISSING)

146
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:17,364
Ed. Please, please,
I can change.

147
00:07:17,537 --> 00:07:19,438
Say you're right,
say you're right.

148
00:07:19,773 --> 00:07:21,733
The fact that I love you
proves that I can change.

149
00:07:21,841 --> 00:07:22,900
Just give me a chance.

150
00:07:23,576 --> 00:07:25,602
You know as well as I
that a man facing death

151
00:07:25,779 --> 00:07:28,772
will say anything to save his
skin. And you won't change.

152
00:07:30,317 --> 00:07:31,478
Because you can't.

153
00:07:34,854 --> 00:07:37,824
I was going to have
you say hello to Isabella,

154
00:07:37,991 --> 00:07:39,084
- but...
- (CHOKING)

155
00:07:39,259 --> 00:07:42,889
I think you are going
to a very different place.

156
00:07:43,163 --> 00:07:45,530
- (GASPS)
- Goodbye, Oswald.

157
00:07:46,967 --> 00:07:47,991
Ed!

158
00:07:48,568 --> 00:07:50,594
Ed! Ed!

159
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:53,405
Okay, I think that's
about all I can do.

160
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,440
Thanks.

161
00:07:55,141 --> 00:07:56,141
How's triage going?

162
00:07:56,309 --> 00:07:57,971
A lot of overflow
from Gotham General.

163
00:07:58,144 --> 00:07:59,203
What do you want?

164
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:02,272
When Jerome woke
up, did he say anything?

165
00:08:02,449 --> 00:08:03,940
Said he wanted his face back.

166
00:08:04,150 --> 00:08:06,710
No. I mean, anything that might
indicate where he was going?

167
00:08:06,886 --> 00:08:08,864
- What he was planning?
- We were just playing catch up.

168
00:08:08,888 --> 00:08:10,433
You know, about coming
back to life. The cult.

169
00:08:10,457 --> 00:08:12,137
He asked if you and
I were still together.

170
00:08:12,258 --> 00:08:14,203
I mentioned you killed my
husband on our wedding night.

171
00:08:14,227 --> 00:08:15,371
And he thought
that was hilarious

172
00:08:15,395 --> 00:08:18,092
so that's something the two of you
can bond over when you find him.

173
00:08:22,202 --> 00:08:23,295
He didn't tell me his plan.

174
00:08:23,470 --> 00:08:25,150
He talked about
Galavan, the night he died.

175
00:08:25,205 --> 00:08:26,468
And then he mentioned...

176
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:28,608
- What?
- Bruce.

177
00:08:29,075 --> 00:08:30,252
He said the last
thing he remembers

178
00:08:30,276 --> 00:08:31,787
is that he was gonna
kill Bruce Wayne.

179
00:08:31,811 --> 00:08:33,302
Call Alfred. Tell
him I'm on my way.

180
00:08:36,583 --> 00:08:38,484
- I'll light these candles.
- Good lad.

181
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:41,732
I'll go downstairs to see if there's
any life left in that old generator.

182
00:08:42,722 --> 00:08:43,951
(TELEPHONE RINGING)

183
00:08:46,159 --> 00:08:47,239
Who's calling at this hour?

184
00:08:59,239 --> 00:09:00,263
Alfred?

185
00:09:01,908 --> 00:09:03,240
(GRUNTING)

186
00:09:07,847 --> 00:09:10,043
(JEROME LAUGHING MOCKINGLY)

187
00:09:11,017 --> 00:09:13,452
Ooh!

188
00:09:17,724 --> 00:09:18,851
My, my.

189
00:09:21,094 --> 00:09:22,460
Look how big you've gotten.

190
00:09:22,962 --> 00:09:23,962
(LAUGHS)

191
00:09:29,102 --> 00:09:31,003
- (MEN CHATTERING)
- (GLASS SHATTERING)

192
00:09:31,871 --> 00:09:32,964
Are you okay?

193
00:09:33,139 --> 00:09:35,165
I'll be fine, Master
Bruce. I'll be fine.

194
00:09:36,609 --> 00:09:39,044
JEROME: Nice place
you got here. You rent?

195
00:09:39,546 --> 00:09:41,174
- What do you want?
- (GLASS SHATTERING)

196
00:09:41,915 --> 00:09:42,915
Attitude.

197
00:09:44,517 --> 00:09:45,815
Teenagers, am I right?

198
00:09:46,319 --> 00:09:48,584
Oh, I remember those days.

199
00:09:48,755 --> 00:09:51,247
So many exciting new
emotions floating through you.

200
00:09:51,424 --> 00:09:54,223
Wanting to kill
everyone you saw.

201
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:55,427
Oh...

202
00:09:58,731 --> 00:10:00,461
You. Give me.

203
00:10:04,137 --> 00:10:06,663
You know, I will never
understand rich people's tastes.

204
00:10:06,840 --> 00:10:09,674
It's worthless. My father
found it at a flea market.

205
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:12,845
<i>- I keep it for sentimental reasons.</i>
- Nice try.

206
00:10:13,346 --> 00:10:14,837
Oh, it's got some heft to it.

207
00:10:15,014 --> 00:10:17,245
Expensive, I'm guessing.
It'd be such a shame if I...

208
00:10:17,417 --> 00:10:18,441
No! Don't...

209
00:10:18,952 --> 00:10:19,952
JEROME: Oh...

210
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:24,648
Tougher than I figured. Anyway.

211
00:10:26,459 --> 00:10:28,052
Oh, bloody hell.

212
00:10:28,228 --> 00:10:31,357
- I asked you what you want.
- Right. Sorry.

213
00:10:31,531 --> 00:10:34,023
The old noodle's still a
little al dente post thaw.

214
00:10:34,467 --> 00:10:36,561
The reason I'm here
is I'm gonna kill you.

215
00:10:38,638 --> 00:10:39,901
- Why?
<i>- Well,</i>

216
00:10:40,406 --> 00:10:42,136
just last thing I
remember wanting to do.

217
00:10:43,109 --> 00:10:45,408
It's been nagging at
me since I woke up.

218
00:10:47,914 --> 00:10:53,319
The idea of slitting that
pretty, pink throat of yours.

219
00:10:53,620 --> 00:10:56,522
Figure that'll clear the
decks. What do you think?

220
00:10:57,323 --> 00:10:58,416
- Don't you...
- (GUN COCKS)

221
00:10:58,658 --> 00:10:59,853
I remember that night.

222
00:11:00,627 --> 00:11:03,893
When you took over the benefit.
You were quite the showman.

223
00:11:04,297 --> 00:11:06,357
Thank you. Always
nice being appreciated.

224
00:11:06,533 --> 00:11:08,053
And you're just
going to kill me here.

225
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:10,682
It's kind of disappointing.

226
00:11:18,745 --> 00:11:20,043
Ah, what do you mean?

227
00:11:20,213 --> 00:11:22,705
After all the buildup,
you coming back to life,

228
00:11:23,082 --> 00:11:24,402
turning off the
lights in Gotham,

229
00:11:24,551 --> 00:11:26,952
killing me here just
doesn't show a lot of...

230
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:33,225
Flair? Style? Panache? Hmm?

231
00:11:34,894 --> 00:11:36,829
Go on, boy, spit
it out. I can take it.

232
00:11:37,363 --> 00:11:39,161
- I'm Bruce Wayne.
- I'm aware.

233
00:11:39,332 --> 00:11:40,857
I am the ruling elite.

234
00:11:41,034 --> 00:11:44,903
My company is the machine that
keeps the cogs of Gotham running.

235
00:11:45,171 --> 00:11:46,171
Wow.

236
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:48,269
Killing me should
mean something.

237
00:11:48,441 --> 00:11:50,281
And you're telling me
no one's going to see it?

238
00:11:52,212 --> 00:11:53,805
You're saying I
need an audience?

239
00:11:55,114 --> 00:11:56,114
Oh...

240
00:11:56,316 --> 00:12:01,084
Look, I know you're just trying
to buy time so you can escape.

241
00:12:02,789 --> 00:12:04,553
But your point is still valid.

242
00:12:05,592 --> 00:12:08,255
Saddle up, boys. We're
taking this show on the road.

243
00:12:08,428 --> 00:12:11,364
And I know just
the spot. Come on.

244
00:12:11,564 --> 00:12:12,588
Eh-eh-eh.

245
00:12:12,832 --> 00:12:14,027
Not you, old chap.

246
00:12:14,367 --> 00:12:16,700
The prince of Gotham
deserves a public death.

247
00:12:16,869 --> 00:12:18,735
His butler? Not
so much. Kill him.

248
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,066
- No!
- Bruce!

249
00:12:22,909 --> 00:12:24,429
This is what you've
been training for.

250
00:12:25,778 --> 00:12:27,298
You're gonna be
all right on your own.

251
00:12:31,317 --> 00:12:32,717
I will see you again.

252
00:12:34,187 --> 00:12:35,780
You carry on, son, you carry on.

253
00:12:37,056 --> 00:12:40,049
Strangely intimate.
Come on. Mmm.

254
00:12:40,493 --> 00:12:42,013
Try not to get any
blood on the couch.

255
00:12:42,128 --> 00:12:43,208
<i>I might come back for that.</i>

256
00:12:43,997 --> 00:12:46,057
COBBLEPOT: (GASPING) <i>Help!</i>

257
00:12:46,232 --> 00:12:49,498
Somebody help me! Help!

258
00:12:51,537 --> 00:12:52,698
(SCREAMING)

259
00:12:53,273 --> 00:12:54,273
(ACID SIZZLING)

260
00:12:56,342 --> 00:12:57,503
- Help!
- MAN: <i>Hello?</i>

261
00:12:57,977 --> 00:12:59,673
(GASPING) Over here!

262
00:13:00,179 --> 00:13:01,179
Oh! (LAUGHS)

263
00:13:01,381 --> 00:13:02,381
Oh, thank God.

264
00:13:02,548 --> 00:13:04,847
There's not much time!
Cut me loose! Hurry!

265
00:13:05,018 --> 00:13:07,920
- What's that car doing here?
- Does it matter? Cut me loose.

266
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:10,886
- Hey, you, you look familiar.
- Oh, yes.

267
00:13:11,057 --> 00:13:12,491
I happen to be the
Mayor of Gotham.

268
00:13:12,659 --> 00:13:13,888
So, free me.

269
00:13:14,060 --> 00:13:16,052
And I promise there will
be a handsome reward.

270
00:13:16,229 --> 00:13:19,199
Holy... It really is you. The
Mayor of Gotham, in the flesh.

271
00:13:19,365 --> 00:13:22,233
Yes! Now stop standing
there and get me out of here!

272
00:13:23,002 --> 00:13:24,129
I don't... I don't know.

273
00:13:24,671 --> 00:13:25,866
- What did you do?
- What?

274
00:13:26,039 --> 00:13:28,372
Oh, I'm gonna die here
listening to this moron.

275
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:31,534
- Just cut the ropes!
- Okay, okay, okay.

276
00:13:32,412 --> 00:13:33,903
(GASPING) Oh, God.

277
00:13:37,517 --> 00:13:38,780
- Hurry!
- Yeah.

278
00:13:47,060 --> 00:13:50,121
(COBBLEPOT CONTINUES GASPING)

279
00:13:52,632 --> 00:13:53,998
(GLASS SHATTERING)

280
00:13:56,436 --> 00:13:58,064
MAN: <i>Whoopsie!</i> (LAUGHS)

281
00:13:58,738 --> 00:14:01,071
Fine, come on then.
What are you waiting for?

282
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:02,833
MAN 1: <i>You in a
rush to die, old man?</i>

283
00:14:03,443 --> 00:14:04,953
<i>Who's gonna kill him?
Who's gonna do him?</i>

284
00:14:04,977 --> 00:14:07,572
- MAN 2: <i>I'll do him.</i>
- What? What, you three?

285
00:14:08,348 --> 00:14:11,409
You three left here to take
out the rubbish, were ya?

286
00:14:11,584 --> 00:14:13,780
You, Mr. Machine gun
with the suits of armor,

287
00:14:13,953 --> 00:14:15,331
I want you to shoot
me in the grill, are ya?

288
00:14:15,355 --> 00:14:17,035
How about you with
the crowbar by the sofa?

289
00:14:17,156 --> 00:14:21,321
Gonna cave in my skull? And
how about you, Mr. Machete?

290
00:14:21,627 --> 00:14:23,005
Oh, come on in,
Sunshine, don't be shy.

291
00:14:23,029 --> 00:14:24,429
Your mama wasn't. Chop, chop.

292
00:14:24,597 --> 00:14:26,828
- Who're you talking to, old man?
- JIM: <i>Me.</i>

293
00:14:37,777 --> 00:14:38,777
(GROANS)

294
00:14:39,178 --> 00:14:40,202
(GRUNTING)

295
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:43,048
(GROANING)

296
00:14:47,387 --> 00:14:49,947
- Where's Bruce?
- That lunatic Jerome took him.

297
00:14:52,225 --> 00:14:53,750
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

298
00:14:53,993 --> 00:14:55,222
(GUNFIRE NEARBY)

299
00:14:57,663 --> 00:14:59,291
(CARNIVAL MUSIC PLAYING)

300
00:15:06,739 --> 00:15:07,739
(EXHALES)

301
00:15:23,423 --> 00:15:24,423
(MAN GASPS)

302
00:15:24,724 --> 00:15:27,091
- (MEN LAUGHING)
- WOMAN: No, please. No.

303
00:15:27,326 --> 00:15:28,937
- (WOMAN GROANING)
- (MEN CONTINUE LAUGHING)

304
00:15:28,961 --> 00:15:29,985
(GRUNTS)

305
00:15:31,898 --> 00:15:33,230
(INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

306
00:15:40,773 --> 00:15:42,605
Get him. Squash her.

307
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:44,777
(MAN GRUNTING)

308
00:15:45,244 --> 00:15:46,712
Get the old lady. Come on.

309
00:15:47,213 --> 00:15:48,909
<i>The fat guy. Put
your back into it.</i>

310
00:15:50,850 --> 00:15:51,850
Oh.

311
00:15:54,487 --> 00:15:55,819
(JEROME CHUCKLES)

312
00:15:56,088 --> 00:15:58,148
<i>Well, we're off to a good start.</i>

313
00:15:59,826 --> 00:16:00,953
What do you say, Bruce?

314
00:16:02,161 --> 00:16:04,596
Wanna have some fun
before the main event?

315
00:16:15,641 --> 00:16:17,401
Bullock's pulling
messages from the tip line.

316
00:16:18,311 --> 00:16:19,888
You said Bruce was
able to convince Jerome

317
00:16:19,912 --> 00:16:21,190
to kill him in front
of an audience?

318
00:16:21,214 --> 00:16:23,094
Yeah, he's trying to buy
himself some more time.

319
00:16:23,449 --> 00:16:25,611
I would be proud if I
wasn't so bloody terrified.

320
00:16:27,553 --> 00:16:28,873
<i>City's given way
to Bedlam again.</i>

321
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:30,221
Get down. Get in. Oh, shut up.

322
00:16:30,389 --> 00:16:32,824
Jerome's acolytes have
occupied places all over town, so

323
00:16:33,459 --> 00:16:35,019
finding an audience
won't be the issue.

324
00:16:35,194 --> 00:16:37,186
- The question is where.
- BULLOCK: <i>We got him.</i>

325
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:39,792
They're in Anders
Park, the cathedral,

326
00:16:40,099 --> 00:16:42,534
the zoo, they've taken over
the Hillside Conservatory,

327
00:16:42,702 --> 00:16:44,967
the Courthouse and
The Boardwalk Circus.

328
00:16:45,605 --> 00:16:47,039
Jerome was raised in a circus.

329
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,518
Have a Strike Force and all
available units meet us there.

330
00:16:49,542 --> 00:16:51,477
I'll put out the call
on the way. Let's roll.

331
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,246
(EXCITED CHATTER)

332
00:16:59,919 --> 00:17:01,888
Gotta be honest, Bruce,

333
00:17:02,054 --> 00:17:05,218
you don't make the
world's funniest clown.

334
00:17:06,025 --> 00:17:07,025
But...

335
00:17:07,393 --> 00:17:08,393
MAN: Ooh!

336
00:17:08,895 --> 00:17:09,988
We can fix that.

337
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:13,865
(GROANING)

338
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:16,161
(JEROME EXHALES)

339
00:17:16,369 --> 00:17:17,679
- (MAN GRUNTING)
- (FLESH SQUELCHING)

340
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,569
Ah, shut up, you big baby.

341
00:17:21,908 --> 00:17:25,208
Let's turn that
frown upside down.

342
00:17:28,214 --> 00:17:29,214
Gabe!

343
00:17:29,382 --> 00:17:31,647
We need have to find
Ed Nygma and kill him!

344
00:17:32,151 --> 00:17:33,949
- (WHIP CRACKS)
- Gabe, where... (CHOKING)

345
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:36,716
Your monkeys cleared out.

346
00:17:37,657 --> 00:17:39,377
Now what's that you
were saying about Nygma?

347
00:17:40,326 --> 00:17:42,646
Looks like we're not the
only ones trying to kill that guy.

348
00:17:43,362 --> 00:17:44,921
- Now, where is he?
- F...

349
00:17:45,531 --> 00:17:48,365
- I'm sorry, what? Speak up.
- (GASPING)

350
00:17:48,568 --> 00:17:51,128
- What are you doing in my house?
- TABITHA: <i>Whatever we want.</i>

351
00:17:52,138 --> 00:17:54,903
You're finished, Oswald.
Now, where's Nygma?

352
00:17:55,074 --> 00:17:56,133
I don't know.

353
00:17:58,110 --> 00:17:59,110
Think.

354
00:17:59,812 --> 00:18:01,747
- What?
- I said, think!

355
00:18:02,048 --> 00:18:04,279
Oh, I heard you. I'm just
surprised you knew the word.

356
00:18:04,483 --> 00:18:07,647
(LAUGHS) Speaking
of words. Any last ones?

357
00:18:07,820 --> 00:18:10,415
Babs said not to kill
him until we have Nygma.

358
00:18:10,590 --> 00:18:11,888
I don't work for Barbara Kean.

359
00:18:12,391 --> 00:18:13,391
Oh...

360
00:18:14,260 --> 00:18:16,729
Stop pretending that you
are anything but muscle.

361
00:18:16,896 --> 00:18:18,762
Yes, you used to be
someone in Gotham,

362
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:21,366
but those days are
past! (GROANS)

363
00:18:23,569 --> 00:18:24,730
(TABITHA GRUNTS)

364
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:30,001
Remember when I put a
knife in your mom's back?

365
00:18:30,843 --> 00:18:32,277
That was awful, wasn't it?

366
00:18:33,112 --> 00:18:38,141
Her crying, bleeding out, you
just holding her as she died.

367
00:18:39,986 --> 00:18:41,545
And you never did
anything about it.

368
00:18:42,321 --> 00:18:43,345
Yet.

369
00:18:44,824 --> 00:18:47,851
Nah. You had your
chance to kill me.

370
00:18:49,328 --> 00:18:51,524
Stop turning us
against each other.

371
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:56,060
We're taking him with us.

372
00:18:56,402 --> 00:18:59,531
Oh, if you think I am
going anywhere with you...

373
00:18:59,705 --> 00:19:00,705
(GRUNTS)

374
00:19:03,275 --> 00:19:04,795
You realize you have
to carry him now?

375
00:19:05,177 --> 00:19:06,702
Son of a bitch.

376
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,078
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

377
00:19:12,051 --> 00:19:13,485
- (MAN LAUGHING)
- (WOMAN SCREAMS)

378
00:19:13,719 --> 00:19:15,244
MAN: <i>Oh, I missed.</i>

379
00:19:17,289 --> 00:19:19,053
BRUCE: <i>Is there a
plan for all this madness?</i>

380
00:19:19,225 --> 00:19:22,457
These people don't want a
plan, they want an excuse.

381
00:19:23,195 --> 00:19:26,393
A mother who dreams
of strangling her child.

382
00:19:27,066 --> 00:19:29,160
Husband who
wants to stab his wife.

383
00:19:29,602 --> 00:19:31,935
All they want is
someone to tell them...

384
00:19:33,439 --> 00:19:34,439
"Do it."

385
00:19:35,274 --> 00:19:37,675
Kill them. It doesn't matter.

386
00:19:39,612 --> 00:19:40,612
It doesn't.

387
00:19:41,180 --> 00:19:43,240
Ohh! I love this
game. One please.

388
00:19:43,416 --> 00:19:44,416
MAN: <i>You, sir.</i>

389
00:19:45,184 --> 00:19:48,643
<i>No, no, no. Please.
No, no. No, no.</i>

390
00:19:49,522 --> 00:19:52,356
- You won't get away with it.
- Already did. Now, shush.

391
00:19:52,792 --> 00:19:53,816
Need to concentrate.

392
00:19:54,093 --> 00:19:55,288
(GRUNTS, SPITS)

393
00:19:55,594 --> 00:19:58,274
A few dozen brainwashed maniacs
can't keep the city hostage forever.

394
00:19:58,397 --> 00:19:59,729
Well, duh.

395
00:20:01,801 --> 00:20:02,962
So, what's the point?

396
00:20:05,805 --> 00:20:06,805
The point

397
00:20:07,573 --> 00:20:11,943
is that all these people out
here, looting, robbing, killing...

398
00:20:13,245 --> 00:20:16,409
They're the people who wash
your car, who pour your coffee,

399
00:20:16,582 --> 00:20:18,483
who take out your trash.

400
00:20:18,651 --> 00:20:21,553
<i>And what happened the
moment the lights went out?</i>

401
00:20:22,254 --> 00:20:23,722
They showed their true faces.

402
00:20:25,057 --> 00:20:28,118
They showed how quickly
they want to open up

403
00:20:28,294 --> 00:20:32,561
your rich boy veins and
bathe in your blue blood.

404
00:20:32,732 --> 00:20:34,758
That is the point.

405
00:20:35,201 --> 00:20:36,201
That's not true.

406
00:20:38,104 --> 00:20:39,766
There are good people in Gotham.

407
00:20:40,206 --> 00:20:42,334
(LAUGHING)

408
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:46,010
Like who?

409
00:20:46,178 --> 00:20:50,343
The sheep who locked their
doors and crawled under their beds?

410
00:20:51,283 --> 00:20:52,307
Face it, kid.

411
00:20:53,552 --> 00:20:55,612
Gotham has no heroes.

412
00:21:02,695 --> 00:21:04,288
- MAN: <i>No. No, no!</i>
- Wait.

413
00:21:04,463 --> 00:21:05,487
Hey.

414
00:21:06,098 --> 00:21:07,098
Foul!

415
00:21:08,234 --> 00:21:09,395
He pushed me, you see that?

416
00:21:09,568 --> 00:21:12,595
You wanna kill someone?
Let's get on with it. Come on.

417
00:21:13,405 --> 00:21:15,203
(YAWNS MOCKINGLY)
You're so boring, Bruce.

418
00:21:15,441 --> 00:21:16,704
- (BELL DINGS)
- (SCREAMING)

419
00:21:16,976 --> 00:21:17,976
No!

420
00:21:21,147 --> 00:21:23,616
Oh. Sorry. You.

421
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,144
(EXHALES)

422
00:21:29,321 --> 00:21:31,313
(GRUNTING)

423
00:21:34,760 --> 00:21:36,251
(GROANS WEAKLY)

424
00:21:36,462 --> 00:21:37,486
Did that hurt?

425
00:21:39,999 --> 00:21:40,999
Not much.

426
00:21:42,268 --> 00:21:44,328
- You try.
- (STAPLER CLICKS)

427
00:21:53,445 --> 00:21:54,936
- Stop!
- (LAUGHS)

428
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,378
- Stop!
- All right.

429
00:21:58,450 --> 00:22:01,648
Enough dilly-dally.
To the main event.

430
00:22:16,669 --> 00:22:18,934
- Where the hell is our backup?
- Still two minutes out.

431
00:22:19,104 --> 00:22:21,505
Most were waylaid by
another riot on the west side.

432
00:22:21,674 --> 00:22:23,434
- Yeah, but we can't wait, mate.
- All right.

433
00:22:23,576 --> 00:22:25,875
So, we go in,

434
00:22:26,312 --> 00:22:30,272
find Bruce, get him to safety.
Then we go after Jerome. Ready?

435
00:22:30,449 --> 00:22:31,473
Not really.

436
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:35,351
- (PEOPLE SHOUTING)
- MAN: <i>We all know why we're here.</i>

437
00:22:35,521 --> 00:22:38,719
<i>Here comes Jerome!
Everybody!</i> (LAUGHS)

438
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,356
(CROWD CHEERING)

439
00:22:52,071 --> 00:22:54,540
(OVER MEGAPHONE) <i>Hear
ye! Hear ye! Gather round.</i>

440
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:58,769
<i>The show is about to begin!</i>

441
00:22:59,311 --> 00:23:00,711
(CROWD CHEERING)

442
00:23:05,551 --> 00:23:08,020
(MAN WHOOPING AND LAUGHING)

443
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:10,412
MAN: <i>Let me hear it.</i>

444
00:23:11,757 --> 00:23:13,419
Come on now. Come on.

445
00:23:14,593 --> 00:23:15,593
(CROWD GASPS)

446
00:23:15,794 --> 00:23:16,887
<i>Shut up!</i>

447
00:23:17,162 --> 00:23:18,162
(LAUGHTER)

448
00:23:18,464 --> 00:23:20,933
<i>Better.</i> (LAUGHS)

449
00:23:22,534 --> 00:23:27,199
<i>Well, I think we can all agree
tonight was a rousing success.</i>

450
00:23:27,940 --> 00:23:32,173
<i>We brought this
miserable city to its knees.</i>

451
00:23:32,511 --> 00:23:33,740
(CROWD CHEERING)

452
00:23:35,314 --> 00:23:40,014
<i>So, how to thank the
best darn cult of fanatics</i>

453
00:23:40,185 --> 00:23:43,349
<i>a messiah like myself
could ever hope for?</i>

454
00:23:43,522 --> 00:23:44,615
<i>I give you...</i>

455
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:46,187
(FANFARE PLAYS)

456
00:23:48,127 --> 00:23:49,127
<i>Cue!</i>

457
00:23:49,628 --> 00:23:50,628
Oh...

458
00:23:52,097 --> 00:23:53,292
(CROWD CHEERING)

459
00:23:53,532 --> 00:23:57,697
JEROME: <i>I give you the
climax of our festivities.</i>

460
00:23:57,870 --> 00:24:00,237
<i>The billionaire
prince of Gotham,</i>

461
00:24:00,406 --> 00:24:06,346
<i>Bruce Wayne!</i>

462
00:24:12,551 --> 00:24:15,020
<i>Well, so what do you say, Bruce?</i>

463
00:24:15,554 --> 00:24:21,050
<i>Shall we end the night with a
bang? Or better yet, a boom?</i>

464
00:24:23,062 --> 00:24:24,894
(CARNIVAL MUSIC PLAYING)

465
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:37,538
CROWD: Boom! Boom! Boom! Boom!

466
00:24:37,710 --> 00:24:39,702
Boom! Boom! Boom!

467
00:24:43,549 --> 00:24:44,710
(STRAINING)

468
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,353
All right.

469
00:24:51,056 --> 00:24:52,056
What's next?

470
00:24:54,093 --> 00:24:57,120
Death by 1,000 cuts.
Very poetic. I like it.

471
00:25:02,368 --> 00:25:03,392
So nice.

472
00:25:07,006 --> 00:25:08,030
Nailed it.

473
00:25:15,881 --> 00:25:17,645
<i>All right, folks, this
is very important,</i>

474
00:25:17,816 --> 00:25:21,446
<i>whatever you do, please
definitely try this at home.</i>

475
00:25:21,620 --> 00:25:23,088
<i>Preferably on a family member.</i>

476
00:25:23,422 --> 00:25:24,422
(GRUNTS)

477
00:25:24,656 --> 00:25:25,885
(CROWD LAUGHING)

478
00:25:26,058 --> 00:25:27,082
Yeah.

479
00:25:27,359 --> 00:25:29,260
(CROWD CHEERING)

480
00:25:36,935 --> 00:25:39,029
- You ready, partner?
- Oh, good Lord.

481
00:25:39,538 --> 00:25:41,458
The Strike Force just
arrived. They're coming in.

482
00:25:48,647 --> 00:25:49,842
Detective Gordon!

483
00:25:50,015 --> 00:25:51,575
You're just in time
for the big finish.

484
00:25:51,750 --> 00:25:52,843
JIM: <i>Nobody move!</i>

485
00:26:00,559 --> 00:26:01,720
(GUNFIRE)

486
00:26:06,098 --> 00:26:07,623
(BULLET RICOCHETS)

487
00:26:10,702 --> 00:26:11,702
(LAUGHS)

488
00:26:19,845 --> 00:26:20,845
(GRUNTS)

489
00:26:26,785 --> 00:26:27,785
(GUNFIRE CONTINUES)

490
00:26:44,837 --> 00:26:45,837
(GRUNTS)

491
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:02,811
Find him. I'll find Jerome.

492
00:27:04,857 --> 00:27:07,258
- (SIREN WAILING)
- (INDISTINCT SHOUTING)

493
00:27:09,027 --> 00:27:10,027
So.

494
00:27:12,131 --> 00:27:13,131
Here we are.

495
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:16,835
I suppose I underestimated
you, Barbara.

496
00:27:17,002 --> 00:27:19,494
- It's the curse of great beauty.
- How did it go?

497
00:27:20,806 --> 00:27:22,726
You put together what
happened to Ed's librarian,

498
00:27:23,275 --> 00:27:26,677
- turned him against me.
- Honestly, wasn't too hard.

499
00:27:27,813 --> 00:27:30,612
And then together you hatched a
plan to destroy everything I made

500
00:27:31,617 --> 00:27:33,279
- and kill me?
- Pretty much.

501
00:27:34,686 --> 00:27:38,123
And brother, did
you ever take the bait.

502
00:27:38,757 --> 00:27:40,055
(LAUGHS)

503
00:27:41,059 --> 00:27:43,528
Well, I hope you're happy
at the head of the table.

504
00:27:44,696 --> 00:27:48,428
You know, the table is more or
less littered with dead old dudes,

505
00:27:48,600 --> 00:27:51,126
but hey, it's a place
to grow. (CHUCKLES)

506
00:27:51,303 --> 00:27:54,865
And now you've got what you
want, you don't need Ed anymore.

507
00:27:55,507 --> 00:27:58,033
- Mmm. (CHUCKLES)
- (LAUGHS)

508
00:27:58,310 --> 00:28:00,404
My, my. Didn't take you
long to turn on each other.

509
00:28:00,579 --> 00:28:01,579
(SCOFFS)

510
00:28:01,747 --> 00:28:05,445
You know, I think of it as a limited
partnership that needs dissolving.

511
00:28:07,152 --> 00:28:10,054
So, I help you find Ed,

512
00:28:10,589 --> 00:28:15,289
things go better for
me. I don't, you kill me.

513
00:28:16,962 --> 00:28:17,962
That about it?

514
00:28:19,031 --> 00:28:20,055
Yeah.

515
00:28:20,432 --> 00:28:22,162
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

516
00:28:25,938 --> 00:28:28,635
Oh, Bruce. Where are you, boy?

517
00:28:30,742 --> 00:28:33,712
Come on out,
boy. I won't hurt ya.

518
00:28:38,550 --> 00:28:39,950
Bruce, darling.

519
00:28:46,258 --> 00:28:48,227
Oh, Brucey.

520
00:29:00,472 --> 00:29:02,703
You ruined my show, Bruce.

521
00:29:03,208 --> 00:29:06,235
Hiding's just gonna
make things worse.

522
00:29:10,048 --> 00:29:14,577
I didn't come here to hide.
I wanted you to follow me.

523
00:29:19,725 --> 00:29:21,717
You're going to pay
for what you've done.

524
00:29:30,769 --> 00:29:32,101
You're going to call Ed.

525
00:29:32,271 --> 00:29:33,796
Tell him you're
alive. Tell him...

526
00:29:33,972 --> 00:29:36,601
Oh, I don't care. But
find out where he is.

527
00:29:37,175 --> 00:29:39,667
- Why don't you call him?
- Because he's not stupid.

528
00:29:40,245 --> 00:29:41,605
He knows that now
you're no longer

529
00:29:41,747 --> 00:29:44,182
the head of the
underworld or anything else,

530
00:29:44,583 --> 00:29:47,712
we don't need him
anymore. It is our time to rule.

531
00:29:48,020 --> 00:29:49,020
(SCOFFS)

532
00:29:49,788 --> 00:29:52,348
You understand if I
feel compelled to refuse.

533
00:29:53,292 --> 00:29:55,921
Give me five minutes,
he won't refuse.

534
00:29:56,094 --> 00:29:57,426
I'd do it in three.

535
00:29:57,596 --> 00:29:59,064
- Why you gotta do that?
- What?

536
00:29:59,231 --> 00:30:00,642
Cut me down like
that in front of people.

537
00:30:00,666 --> 00:30:02,794
- I'm just saying...
- Would the two of you shut up?

538
00:30:05,370 --> 00:30:08,272
Give up Nygma. And
save your own ass.

539
00:30:08,807 --> 00:30:11,242
Live to love another day. Hey.

540
00:30:16,715 --> 00:30:17,739
Wow.

541
00:30:19,184 --> 00:30:21,881
What's going on? You have
a weird look on your face.

542
00:30:22,054 --> 00:30:23,215
Like, weirder than normal.

543
00:30:24,656 --> 00:30:25,656
You're right.

544
00:30:27,092 --> 00:30:29,891
- I should want him dead.
- "Should?"

545
00:30:31,863 --> 00:30:32,887
Oswald,

546
00:30:33,865 --> 00:30:37,597
you loved him, and
he betrayed you.

547
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:39,196
Actually, I don't
know that I did.

548
00:30:40,439 --> 00:30:43,375
- Love him. Not really.
- What?

549
00:30:43,809 --> 00:30:44,809
Ed was right.

550
00:30:45,977 --> 00:30:47,809
I thought I loved him

551
00:30:49,981 --> 00:30:52,280
because he saw me as no
one had since my mother.

552
00:30:55,020 --> 00:30:56,147
But I killed Isabelle.

553
00:30:56,321 --> 00:30:58,790
I'm pretty sure her name
is Isabella, but go on.

554
00:31:02,794 --> 00:31:04,057
Because I wouldn't share him.

555
00:31:06,164 --> 00:31:07,723
Ed said love is sacrifice.

556
00:31:09,334 --> 00:31:12,065
I should have been able to
sacrifice my happiness for his.

557
00:31:15,674 --> 00:31:16,674
I couldn't.

558
00:31:19,911 --> 00:31:20,970
But I'm ready now.

559
00:31:21,646 --> 00:31:22,646
(SOBS)

560
00:31:23,148 --> 00:31:25,708
I won't call Ed.

561
00:31:26,551 --> 00:31:28,076
I won't let you hurt him.

562
00:31:28,253 --> 00:31:31,348
So, you'd rather die than give
up the man who tried to kill you?

563
00:31:31,556 --> 00:31:36,460
- (LAUGHS) I would. Isn't that crazy?
- ED: <i>Yes.</i>

564
00:31:39,364 --> 00:31:40,388
It is.

565
00:31:41,433 --> 00:31:43,311
Guess you're not as smart
as you thought you were.

566
00:31:43,335 --> 00:31:44,735
He didn't give you up after all.

567
00:31:48,373 --> 00:31:49,602
You're in this together?

568
00:31:50,208 --> 00:31:51,208
(SIGHS)

569
00:31:51,610 --> 00:31:52,610
But why?

570
00:31:52,778 --> 00:31:55,270
Because I didn't want
to just take what you had.

571
00:31:56,381 --> 00:31:58,350
I wanted to take
what you believed.

572
00:31:59,084 --> 00:32:02,179
I wanted you to die

573
00:32:02,788 --> 00:32:05,883
knowing that you were
incapable of loving another person.

574
00:32:07,859 --> 00:32:11,762
(GASPS) But I can. I
just proved that, right?

575
00:32:13,532 --> 00:32:15,558
Does that mean I
passed? (LAUGHS)

576
00:32:15,867 --> 00:32:17,267
(GASPING)

577
00:32:18,069 --> 00:32:19,069
- Ed?
- I...

578
00:32:21,873 --> 00:32:23,865
Don't know what it means.

579
00:32:24,810 --> 00:32:25,810
(SIGHS)

580
00:32:28,547 --> 00:32:30,243
(GASPS, CHUCKLES)

581
00:32:33,885 --> 00:32:34,885
(EXHALES)

582
00:32:36,721 --> 00:32:38,713
(LAUGHING)

583
00:32:40,826 --> 00:32:42,124
I have to tell you,

584
00:32:43,094 --> 00:32:46,292
this is way more fun
than I was expecting.

585
00:32:52,737 --> 00:32:55,002
We make a good team, you and me.

586
00:32:55,874 --> 00:32:57,399
BRUCE: <i>You killed Alfred.</i>

587
00:32:59,711 --> 00:33:01,145
Is that what this is about?

588
00:33:02,013 --> 00:33:03,013
<i>Yeesh.</i>

589
00:33:03,248 --> 00:33:06,309
Are all rich kids this
close with their butlers?

590
00:33:07,185 --> 00:33:08,185
Oh!

591
00:33:09,721 --> 00:33:11,383
BRUCE: <i>This is about
doing what's right.</i>

592
00:33:11,556 --> 00:33:13,024
You want to be a hero?

593
00:33:13,892 --> 00:33:18,227
Tell you what, buddy, I'll
give you a fighting chance.

594
00:33:19,631 --> 00:33:24,399
Let's do this <i>mano y
mano,</i> my little conquistador.

595
00:33:25,203 --> 00:33:26,227
Come on.

596
00:33:27,873 --> 00:33:29,000
(BOTH GRUNTING)

597
00:33:29,241 --> 00:33:31,335
What kind of hero tackles
someone from behind?

598
00:33:36,481 --> 00:33:37,779
(GRUNTS)

599
00:33:48,226 --> 00:33:49,226
(LAUGHING)

600
00:33:50,462 --> 00:33:54,297
Let it out. That's
it. That's it.

601
00:33:56,668 --> 00:33:59,137
That's it. Let it out.

602
00:34:04,376 --> 00:34:05,400
- Let it out.
- (PANTING)

603
00:34:10,282 --> 00:34:11,282
<i>Do it.</i>

604
00:34:17,923 --> 00:34:18,923
<i>Bruce!</i>

605
00:34:20,091 --> 00:34:21,091
(CHUCKLES)

606
00:34:22,627 --> 00:34:23,627
(GRUNTS SOFTLY)

607
00:34:23,828 --> 00:34:25,763
Do it! (GAGGING)

608
00:34:29,968 --> 00:34:31,561
(SCREAMS)

609
00:34:44,049 --> 00:34:45,312
(GROANING)

610
00:34:46,017 --> 00:34:47,017
(CHUCKLING)

611
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:51,450
(PEOPLE SHOUTING)

612
00:34:53,625 --> 00:34:54,888
(MAN GRUNTS)

613
00:35:01,566 --> 00:35:02,566
Alfred.

614
00:35:05,804 --> 00:35:06,804
Bruce!

615
00:35:13,078 --> 00:35:14,171
I thought you were dead.

616
00:35:14,779 --> 00:35:16,779
You can't get rid of me
that easily, can you, mate?

617
00:35:31,196 --> 00:35:32,220
Behind you!

618
00:35:42,073 --> 00:35:43,073
Ow!

619
00:35:44,643 --> 00:35:46,839
(GROANING)

620
00:35:48,913 --> 00:35:50,074
(EVIL CHUCKLE)

621
00:35:58,123 --> 00:36:00,115
Word of Jerome's
arrest is spreading quick.

622
00:36:01,092 --> 00:36:02,424
The streets are already quieter.

623
00:36:02,594 --> 00:36:05,792
Soon as the docs reattach
his face, he's off to Arkham.

624
00:36:06,131 --> 00:36:07,291
You wish I would've shot him?

625
00:36:07,699 --> 00:36:09,930
Yeah, he'd probably just
come back from the dead again.

626
00:36:10,101 --> 00:36:11,101
Probably.

627
00:36:11,269 --> 00:36:13,349
At least you get to say you
punched a man's face off.

628
00:36:13,471 --> 00:36:14,598
That's something, right?

629
00:36:17,609 --> 00:36:19,578
- Jim?
- Sorry, what?

630
00:36:20,812 --> 00:36:22,747
Come on. Let me
buy you breakfast.

631
00:36:30,021 --> 00:36:32,013
Well, gotta say,

632
00:36:33,525 --> 00:36:35,391
the clown makeup
was way more terrifying

633
00:36:35,560 --> 00:36:37,222
than the damage
underneath, Master Bruce.

634
00:36:38,329 --> 00:36:39,329
(CHUCKLES)

635
00:36:40,398 --> 00:36:42,299
Did I ever tell you
that I don't like clowns?

636
00:36:44,969 --> 00:36:47,905
Well, in a couple of days...

637
00:36:49,674 --> 00:36:51,802
You'll be back to your
old self. I guarantee it.

638
00:36:53,244 --> 00:36:54,644
You ready to tell
me what happened?

639
00:36:58,550 --> 00:36:59,882
When Jerome took me away,

640
00:37:02,487 --> 00:37:04,007
I thought they were
going to kill you.

641
00:37:06,191 --> 00:37:07,511
Should I tell you
what I thought?

642
00:37:11,629 --> 00:37:16,124
I thought how proud I was of you.
Of the man that you've become.

643
00:37:19,404 --> 00:37:20,667
I almost killed him, Alfred.

644
00:37:21,339 --> 00:37:24,901
Yeah, but you didn't, now, did
you? You controlled your anger.

645
00:37:28,980 --> 00:37:30,073
It wasn't just anger.

646
00:37:32,851 --> 00:37:34,376
After everything
Jerome had done,

647
00:37:35,553 --> 00:37:37,317
after all the pain he caused,

648
00:37:38,823 --> 00:37:40,189
the idea of killing him...

649
00:37:41,893 --> 00:37:43,885
- Felt...
- It felt right.

650
00:37:47,599 --> 00:37:48,599
Yes.

651
00:37:50,502 --> 00:37:51,697
It felt like justice.

652
00:37:52,804 --> 00:37:54,364
There's a very fine
line, Master Bruce,

653
00:37:54,506 --> 00:37:58,409
- between justice and vengeance.
- I know.

654
00:38:01,546 --> 00:38:03,066
But that doesn't
mean there isn't one.

655
00:38:03,515 --> 00:38:04,539
No, it doesn't.

656
00:38:04,716 --> 00:38:06,514
I knew where the line
was tonight, Alfred.

657
00:38:07,485 --> 00:38:08,509
I didn't cross it.

658
00:38:13,258 --> 00:38:15,955
- Well, that's the first rule.
- What do you mean?

659
00:38:17,896 --> 00:38:20,136
Now, I started training you
so you could defend yourself.

660
00:38:20,165 --> 00:38:22,134
Well, we're well
past that, aren't we?

661
00:38:22,801 --> 00:38:27,364
But what's all this training for?
What are you gonna do with it?

662
00:38:31,543 --> 00:38:33,205
- I don't know.
- Nor do I.

663
00:38:33,812 --> 00:38:34,973
But if you keep going,

664
00:38:36,881 --> 00:38:38,144
you're gonna need rules.

665
00:38:40,685 --> 00:38:43,712
Rules you cannot
and you will not break.

666
00:38:44,656 --> 00:38:48,559
Never mind what reason, never
mind what the circumstance.

667
00:38:50,328 --> 00:38:51,489
I will not kill.

668
00:38:57,502 --> 00:38:58,629
Say it again.

669
00:39:02,774 --> 00:39:04,037
I will not kill.

670
00:39:08,079 --> 00:39:09,206
Then let's get to work.

671
00:39:30,101 --> 00:39:31,399
KATHRYN: Tonight, was close.

672
00:39:36,474 --> 00:39:38,272
We could have lost
Gotham for good.

673
00:39:39,811 --> 00:39:44,579
Soon, we will act, and
you will be called upon.

674
00:39:47,151 --> 00:39:49,985
I've done a wonderful
job erasing the scars.

675
00:39:50,889 --> 00:39:52,881
- Are you prepared?
- Yes.

676
00:39:54,325 --> 00:39:56,525
But I still don't understand
how I can help save Gotham.

677
00:39:57,662 --> 00:39:58,662
FRANK: <i>Never fear.</i>

678
00:39:59,998 --> 00:40:01,261
You're only part of the plan.

679
00:40:01,633 --> 00:40:04,228
Are you sure about this?

680
00:40:04,602 --> 00:40:07,902
You know what must
happen if he refuses.

681
00:40:08,072 --> 00:40:09,096
I know.

682
00:40:10,441 --> 00:40:11,909
No one refuses the Court.

683
00:40:34,332 --> 00:40:35,493
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

684
00:40:48,046 --> 00:40:49,605
- Uncle Frank?
<i>- Hello, Jim.</i>

685
00:40:50,481 --> 00:40:51,505
It's been a long time.

686
00:40:54,886 --> 00:40:57,219
Ed, I love you.

687
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:00,322
I know you believe that now.

688
00:41:01,793 --> 00:41:03,728
So, you need to listen
to me when I tell you,

689
00:41:03,895 --> 00:41:07,024
by doing this, it
will change you.

690
00:41:07,832 --> 00:41:10,859
- I've killed before, Oswald.
- Not like this.

691
00:41:12,070 --> 00:41:15,905
This won't be a crime of
passion or self-preservation.

692
00:41:17,508 --> 00:41:20,672
This will be the cold-blooded
murder of someone you love.

693
00:41:22,013 --> 00:41:24,448
I don't love you.

694
00:41:26,451 --> 00:41:27,451
(GRUNTS)

695
00:41:29,854 --> 00:41:31,550
You need me, Edward Nygma.

696
00:41:32,423 --> 00:41:33,516
Just as I need you.

697
00:41:33,691 --> 00:41:35,751
You cannot have
one without the other.

698
00:41:37,428 --> 00:41:38,987
You killed Isabella.

699
00:41:39,163 --> 00:41:42,065
- The point is...
- That is the point!

700
00:41:42,700 --> 00:41:44,931
You can't talk your
way out of this, Oswald.

701
00:41:45,103 --> 00:41:48,835
I have wanted you to
suffer as I've suffered.

702
00:41:49,007 --> 00:41:52,569
You killed her. So, you die.

703
00:41:55,480 --> 00:42:00,544
When I met you, you
were a nervous, jittery loser.

704
00:42:01,753 --> 00:42:03,119
You were nothing!

705
00:42:04,055 --> 00:42:06,581
I created Edward Nygma!

706
00:42:07,158 --> 00:42:11,425
And I am the only one in the
world who truly sees you as you are.

707
00:42:13,965 --> 00:42:16,230
Who you can still become.

708
00:42:19,604 --> 00:42:21,402
You can't do this.

709
00:42:25,276 --> 00:42:26,801
Ed, are you listening to me?

710
00:42:29,013 --> 00:42:30,037
I'm listening.

711
00:42:31,649 --> 00:42:33,015
Say something.

712
00:42:39,490 --> 00:42:40,753
I loved her, Oswald.

713
00:42:43,027 --> 00:42:44,825
- And you killed her.
- (GUN FIRES)

714
00:43:05,416 --> 00:43:06,440
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

715
00:43:17,195 --> 00:43:19,221
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

716
00:43:52,263 --> 00:43:53,263
English -SDH
